## Azurite (local Blob/Queue/Table Storage emulator — Del 10) — this is the
## emulator's own local data files, generated the moment it starts. Same
## reasoning as not committing a LocalDB .mdf: it's runtime state, not source.
.azurite/

## Azurite again, but the files it writes when started WITHOUT --location
## (see README.md step 6) — it then dumps its db state straight into the
## current working directory instead of a subfolder: __azurite_db_blob__.json,
## __azurite_db_blob_extent__.json, __azurite_db_queue__.json, etc., plus two
## folders, __blobstorage__/ and __queuestorage__/. Same runtime-state
## reasoning as .azurite/ above — just a different shape depending on how
## Azurite happened to be started.
__azurite*
__blobstorage__/
__queuestorage__/

